HISTNOTES|notes="DUPLICATES/NEAR-DUPES: 'AMster plan moves forwar.txt-DUP' is an explicit n/a duplicate stub. 'Codex contect compaction.txt' and 'Codex contect compaction - Copia.txt' are the same Falcon-authority-packet edit (Copia = copy). 'integration.txt' (04-23) and 'Open Mythos integration.txt' (04-23) are the same OpenMythos 'what the system IS' + file-by-file registration content. Multiple files are the SAME 2000-file-cap work told repeatedly (Garbag collector work / Garbage collector 2 / Gulp fix / finalizing gulp fix / Final debt shows connectors / Garbage and gulp collector...) and the SAME connector-census 544/27/0 (Delta is sealed / 61 syrfaces / 544 cubes / Atlas integration / cude finding comes next / Graph atlas back online). This is genuine iterative sealing, but the count of 'distinct milestones' is smaller than the file count suggests.\n\nEMPTY FILES: 'Last shat.txt' (04-12), 'Novo(a) Text Document (2).txt' (05-14), 'insanity plan.txt' (05-16), and 'I see FREE REALL GENTS 100B.txt' (06-15) are all empty/no-content.\n\nDATE-CLUSTERING ARTIFACT: ~55+ records share ts 2026-04-15. That is almost certainly a stash-extraction/mtime artifact (one export pass), not 55 tranches literally on one calendar day — treat April-15 ordering as unordered-within-month, not a true sequence.\n\nASPIRATIONAL vs DONE (dual-lens): Many 'sealed/green' claims are explicitly SCOPED — planningReady=true but summon_fired=false; PLANNING_READY / NOT_EXECUTION_READY; LOCAL_ONLY_OVERLAY, PROMOTION=DENY_UNTIL_PROOFS; storage-boot perpetually lane_denied_until_proofs. These are honestly-tagged as NOT promoted, so do not read them as live/arrived. The recurring honest caveats to preserve: (1) real Python GNN weights FAIL to load (state_dict/conv1.bias mismatch) even when JS-gate smoke passes green (GNN.txt, GNN attempt.txt) — the 91-99% accuracies are the paper/model spec, not a live-serving proof from this stash; (2) frozen-brain gemma path is a 0-byte socket = name-reference only (Neural Frozen brain interactive); (3) the 1000-PID 'life-test' is a 100/100 TIMEOUT dataset, self-flagged as 'not a success gate' (Attempt 1000); (4) attached model calls repeatedly time out into clean gc/timeout receipts (Real front, 1000 Prism); (5) 'How to think' is an explicit self-audit admitting behavior didn't change (0 of 6 moves executed, never queried live fabric). MEASURED-and-real (owning-gate-backed) items to trust: recall-serve sub-ms 591286 rows PR#8 (tagged MEASURED_ACER, still HELD pending liris cross-verify), Liris recall :4791 benchmark, 198/198 test ladder synced to faa3f6b, cosign chain live heads.\n\nSCOPE/PROVENANCE: 'Cris WORK.txt' (05-27) is third-party PII with zero Asolaria build content (correctly redacted). 'ASOLARIA_REMINDER_2026-03-04' is the only March record and is just a billing reminder — the fabric's actual birth (2026-02-22, per Fable-5 archaeology) predates this stash. 'new model.txt' is a one-line HuggingFace URL. NovaLum-the-device (Nova lum.txt) is a separate QDD product, distinct from NovaLUM-the-encryption-engine — don't conflate.\n\nGAP: no in-stash July build tranches beyond two framing dialogues (07-03); the stash effectively ends its build-record at the 06-23 recall/migration cluster."|json=0|row_hash=e6516abeaf597430
